{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"61de8aa3-af3e-425c-b7e1-08ed1c1dd3c4","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The issue was caused by DynamoDB rejecting **float** values in the `similar` field. The first publish succeeded because the table was empty, so no scores (floats) were written. On the second publish, `related()` produced float scores, leading to the `TypeError` and a 500 response.\n\n**Fix applied**\n- Added `from decimal import Decimal` to `src/app.py`.\n- Updated `similarity()` to compute the score as a float, round it, then convert it to a `Decimal` (`return Decimal(str(raw))`). This makes the score DynamoDB‑compatible.\n- Adjusted the docstring accordingly.\n\nAll existing tests still pass, and subsequent publishes will no longer raise the error.\n\n**See the detailed explanation and the exact changes in the generated artifact:**  \n[ANSWER.md](/Users/valentinakoniukhova/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/61de8aa3-af3e-425c-b7e1-08ed1c1dd3c4/ANSWER.md) – it includes the root cause, the code modifications, and which parts of the colleague’s note were used.\n","duration_seconds":73.402132,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":18734,"output_tokens":5553,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":197056,"total_tokens":24287}}}
